---
// Progressive payment vs resale — money that is gone, decomposed.
//
// The belief under test is "a new launch is easier on cash flow". It is a claim about
// CASH OUT, and cash out is the wrong ledger: it counts principal repayment, which is
// money moved rather than money spent. So this figure shows only money that never comes
// back — interest and rent — over the identical window for both buyers, from the day each
// decides to the day the launch buyer's loan is fully disbursed.
//
// COLOUR IS ONE MEANING: which KIND of money it is (VOICE.md C10). Two tints of a single
// navy ramp rather than two hues, because both parts belong to one total and a hue change
// would imply they differ in kind rather than in category. Nothing here is green or red:
// rent is not "bad money" and interest is not "good money", and the piece's finding is
// that the trade between them depends entirely on the reader's own situation. Segments are
// separated by a white rule and every value is printed, so meaning never rests on colour.
//
// STAMP DUTY IS DEDUCTED FROM BOTH BARS, not drawn. It is S$44,600 either way, so drawing
// it added equal width to both sides and told the reader nothing about the difference —
// while forcing a third tint into the ramp, which pushed adjacent segments to 2.5:1
// against each other (measured). Two segments clear 5:1 against each other and 3:1 against
// the card. The net difference is identical either way, because the duty cancels.
//
// SEGMENTS are emitted from a month-by-month simulation, not hand-typed. The schedule is
// statutory (Housing Developers Rules, First Schedule, clause 5.1, verified 8 Aug 2026);
// the construction dates are our assumption and are the single largest input, which is
// why the figure states them and why SCENARIOS shows what a longer build does. Totals and
// the net difference are recomputed from SEGMENTS below so the prose cannot drift.
const PRICE = 1_500_000;
const RATE = '1.6%';
const TOP_M = 42;
const FULL_DRAW_M = 54;
const RENT_M = 4300;
const DUTY = 44_600; // identical on both sides, so stated rather than drawn

interface Seg { k: string; label: string; v: number }
interface Side { who: string; note: string; segs: Seg[] }

const SIDES: Side[] = [
  {
    who: 'Resale',
    note: 'completes in month 3, lives in it from then',
    segs: [
      { k: 'int', label: 'Interest', v: 72_266 },
      { k: 'rent', label: 'Rent', v: 12_900 },
    ],
  },
  {
    who: 'New launch',
    note: `keys at month ${TOP_M}, rents until then`,
    segs: [
      { k: 'int', label: 'Interest', v: 28_000 },
      { k: 'rent', label: 'Rent', v: 189_200 },
    ],
  },
];

// What moves the answer, in order of how much it moves it. Net = new launch minus resale,
// so a positive number is money the launch buyer spends and the resale buyer does not.
const SCENARIOS = [
  { label: 'Build runs to 4½ years instead of 3½', net: 171_521 },
  { label: 'Base case above', net: 132_034, base: true },
  { label: 'Mortgage rate 3.0% instead of 1.6%', net: 91_775 },
  { label: 'Mortgage rate 4.0% instead of 1.6%', net: 62_329 },
  { label: 'You live rent-free while it is built', net: -44_266 },
];

const tot = (s: Side) => s.segs.reduce((a, b) => a + b.v, 0);
const MAX = Math.max(...SIDES.map(tot));
const NET = tot(SIDES[1]) - tot(SIDES[0]);
const INT_SAVED = SIDES[0].segs[0].v - SIDES[1].segs[0].v;
const RENT_EXTRA = SIDES[1].segs[1].v - SIDES[0].segs[1].v;
const RATIO = RENT_EXTRA / INT_SAVED;
const SMAX = Math.max(...SCENARIOS.map((s) => Math.abs(s.net)));
const n = (v: number) => `S$${Math.round(v).toLocaleString('en-SG')}`;
const pct = (v: number) => (v / MAX) * 100;
---

<figure class="pp">
  <figcaption class="pp-cap">
    <h4>Money that does not come back, over the same {FULL_DRAW_M} months</h4>
    <p>Two buyers, both needing somewhere to live, both paying {n(PRICE)} at {RATE} with 75% borrowed.
    Principal repayment is excluded on purpose: it is money moved, not money spent. Stamp duty is
    excluded too &mdash; it is {n(DUTY)} either way, so it adds equal width to both bars and says
    nothing about the difference.</p>
  </figcaption>

  <div class="pp-legend">
    {SIDES[0].segs.map((s) => (<span class="pp-lg"><i class={`pp-key ${s.k}`}></i>{s.label}</span>))}
  </div>

  {SIDES.map((s) => (
    <div class="pp-block">
      <div class="pp-who"><b>{s.who}</b> <span class="pp-note">{s.note}</span><span class="pp-tot">{n(tot(s))}</span></div>
      <div class="pp-track">
        {s.segs.map((g) => (
          <span class={`pp-seg ${g.k}`} style={`width:${pct(g.v)}%`}
            role="img" aria-label={`${s.who}: ${g.label} ${n(g.v)}.`}></span>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="pp-vals">
        {s.segs.map((g) => (<span class="pp-v"><i class={`pp-key ${g.k}`}></i>{g.label} {n(g.v)}</span>))}
      </div>
    </div>
  ))}

  <p class="pp-head">The new launch costs <b>{n(NET)}</b> more &mdash; and the two halves of that
  pull in opposite directions. Staging the loan genuinely saves <b>{n(INT_SAVED)}</b> of interest.
  Renting while it is built costs <b>{n(RENT_EXTRA)}</b>, about <b>{RATIO.toFixed(1)} times</b> the saving.</p>

  <div class="pp-sc">
    <div class="pp-sch">What moves the answer &mdash; net difference, new launch minus resale</div>
    <ol class="pp-scrows">
      {SCENARIOS.map((s) => (
        <li class={`pp-scrow${s.base ? ' is-base' : ''}`}>
          <span class="pp-sclab">{s.label}</span>
          <span class="pp-scbar">
            <span class="pp-sczero"></span>
            <span class={`pp-scfill ${s.net < 0 ? 'neg' : 'pos'}`}
              style={`width:${(Math.abs(s.net) / SMAX) * 50}%;${s.net < 0 ? 'right:50%' : 'left:50%'}`}
              role="img"
              aria-label={`${s.label}: the new launch costs ${n(Math.abs(s.net))} ${s.net < 0 ? 'less' : 'more'}.`}></span>
          </span>
          {/* A real minus sign, not "&minus;": an HTML entity inside a JSX expression is
              escaped and renders as its own source text. */}
          <span class="pp-scval">{s.net > 0 ? '+' : '−'}{n(Math.abs(s.net)).replace('S$', '')}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
    <p class="pp-scnote">Bars run left and right of the same centre line, so direction is readable
    without colour. The interest saving grows with the mortgage rate while the rent does not &mdash;
    which is why the new launch looks <em>worse</em> the cheaper borrowing gets, and why the one
    scenario that flips the sign is not about money markets at all.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="pp-src">Computed by us. The instalment schedule is statutory &mdash; Housing Developers
  Rules, First Schedule, clause 5.1 &mdash; and is the same for every uncompleted private home in
  Singapore. Rent is the median district gross yield applied to an equal home, {n(RENT_M)} a month
  here. <b>The construction period is an assumption and is the largest input on the page</b>: nothing
  is published, so we use {TOP_M} months to keys and {FULL_DRAW_M} to the final payment, and show
  above what a year longer does. Interest is charged on the drawn balance only until the loan is
  fully disbursed. Both loans run 30 years; the launch loan simply starts later. Renovation,
  maintenance, property tax and agent fees are excluded from both sides.</p>
</figure>

<style is:global>
.pp{
  /* One ramp, two stops: parts of one total, not two different kinds of thing.
     Measured against each other 5.1:1, and each against the white card 16.8:1 and 3.3:1. */
  --pp-int:#0B1D33; --pp-rent:#7C8FA6;
  --pp-ink:var(--color-dark); --pp-body:var(--color-body); --pp-muted:var(--color-muted);
  --pp-rule:var(--color-border);
  --pp-mono:var(--font-mono),'SF Mono',Menlo,Consolas,monospace;
  margin:26px 0;padding:20px 22px 16px;background:#fff;
  border:1px solid var(--pp-rule);border-radius:12px
}
/* No dark-scheme override: the card is pinned white in both schemes, so the ink follows
   the card rather than the page. Lightening these tints would put pale ink on white. */
.post-content .pp-cap{margin:0 0 14px;padding:0;text-align:left}
.post-content .pp-cap h4{margin:0 0 3px;font-size:15.5px;font-weight:700;color:var(--pp-ink);
  font-family:var(--font-body);letter-spacing:0}
.post-content .pp-cap p{margin:0;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--pp-muted);line-height:1.5}

.pp-legend{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px 16px;align-items:center;margin-bottom:14px;font-size:11.5px}
.pp-lg{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;color:var(--pp-body)}
.pp-key{width:11px;height:11px;border-radius:2px;display:inline-block;flex:0 0 auto}
.pp-key.int{background:var(--pp-int)} .pp-key.rent{background:var(--pp-rent)}

.pp-block{margin-bottom:14px}
.pp-who{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:baseline;gap:8px;font-size:12.5px;
  color:var(--pp-muted);margin-bottom:5px}
.pp-who b{color:var(--pp-ink);font-size:13px}
.pp-note{flex:1 1 auto}
.pp-tot{font-family:var(--pp-mono);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;font-weight:700;
  color:var(--pp-ink);font-size:12.5px;margin-left:auto}
.pp-track{display:flex;height:22px;border-radius:3px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--color-light)}
.pp-seg{display:block;height:22px;min-width:2px;box-shadow:inset -1px 0 0 #fff}
.pp-seg.int{background:var(--pp-int)} .pp-seg.rent{background:var(--pp-rent)}
.pp-vals{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:4px 14px;margin-top:6px;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--pp-body)}
.pp-v{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:5px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}

.post-content p.pp-head{margin:16px 0 0;padding-top:12px;border-top:1px solid var(--pp-rule);
  font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--pp-body)}

.pp-sc{margin-top:16px;padding:12px 14px;border:1px dashed var(--pp-rule);border-radius:8px}
.pp-sch{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;
  color:var(--pp-muted);margin-bottom:10px}
.post-content ol.pp-scrows{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:grid;gap:5px}
.post-content ol.pp-scrows li{margin:0;padding:0}
/* The theme paints a numbered badge on every .post-content ol li, absolutely positioned
   at the left edge, which would land on top of these rows. */
.post-content ol.pp-scrows li::before{content:none;display:none}
.pp-scrow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(96px,190px) 1fr 62px;gap:10px;align-items:center}
.pp-scrow.is-base .pp-sclab{color:var(--pp-ink);font-weight:600}
.pp-sclab{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--pp-body);line-height:1.3}
.pp-scbar{position:relative;height:14px;min-width:0}
.pp-sczero{position:absolute;left:50%;top:-1px;bottom:-1px;width:1px;background:var(--pp-muted);opacity:.6}
.pp-scfill{position:absolute;top:1px;height:12px;background:var(--pp-int);border-radius:2px;min-width:2px}
.pp-scval{font-family:var(--pp-mono);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;font-size:11.5px;
  font-weight:600;color:var(--pp-ink);text-align:right}
.post-content p.pp-scnote{margin:10px 0 0;font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--pp-muted)}

.post-content p.pp-src{margin:12px 0 0;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid var(--pp-rule);
  font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--pp-muted)}

@media (max-width:640px){
  .pp{padding:16px 14px 13px}
  .pp-scrow{grid-template-columns:minmax(84px,130px) 1fr 54px;gap:8px}
  .pp-note{display:none}      /* the timing is in the prose and in each bar's aria-label */
  .pp-sch{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.04em}
}
</style>
